WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:47.841
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:48.111 --> 00:55.076
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

3
00:56.161 --> 00:57.162
Wait…

4
00:57.245 --> 00:59.038
EPISODE 5

5
01:00.623 --> 01:01.457
Unbelievable.

6
01:02.041 --> 01:03.835
I went out of my way to call him.

7
01:05.128 --> 01:07.005
I spoke to him in English

8
01:07.088 --> 01:09.966
so the operator wouldn't understand, but he didn't even thank me.

9
01:16.890 --> 01:17.849
My goodness.

10
01:17.932 --> 01:19.184
You scared me.

11
01:19.684 --> 01:21.019
Why are you standing here?

12
01:22.437 --> 01:23.396
Are you going home?

13
01:23.479 --> 01:26.024
Sorry? You told me to leave for the day.

14
01:27.150 --> 01:29.277
I forgot I was supposed to treat you well.

15
01:30.361 --> 01:32.572
-Let's go to the photo studio. -The photo studio?

16
01:32.655 --> 01:34.824
I'm going with you to the photo studio.

17
01:35.742 --> 01:39.329
Well, I suppose a photo studio picture is better than a newspaper one.

18
01:40.163 --> 01:41.331
Let's go. Come with me.

19
03:02.495 --> 03:04.080
Where are they shooting from?

20
03:04.163 --> 03:05.248
Where did it come from?

21
04:15.151 --> 04:16.110
Are you all right?

22
04:21.991 --> 04:23.076
Get in!

23
04:25.828 --> 04:26.662
Let's go.

24
04:29.624 --> 04:31.626
Damn it. Get in!

25
04:40.885 --> 04:41.886
Get in!

26
04:56.609 --> 04:58.403
Jeong-yeop, stay awake.

27
04:58.486 --> 05:00.154
You have to stay awake.

28
05:01.072 --> 05:02.198
Wake up, you punk!

29
05:03.324 --> 05:05.493
Jeong-yeop!

30
05:13.918 --> 05:14.752
Chief!

31
05:33.729 --> 05:35.106
Over there!

32
06:04.510 --> 06:05.386
Break it!

33
06:12.310 --> 06:13.311
Second floor, go!

34
06:23.196 --> 06:24.113
He went that way.

35
06:28.284 --> 06:29.535
He ran out that way.

36
06:30.578 --> 06:33.122
It's a tall, young guy with a mask on.

37
06:52.850 --> 06:53.851
There's no one here.

38
06:58.648 --> 06:59.815
-That way. -Yes, sir!

39
07:42.984 --> 07:44.068
What do we have here?

40
07:45.570 --> 07:47.029
Close the curtains!

41
07:47.613 --> 07:49.991
She's the daughter of the president of Joil Textile Factory.

42
08:04.714 --> 08:06.048
Joil Textile Factory.

43
08:06.632 --> 08:08.551
She came to get custom clothes fitted.

44
08:08.634 --> 08:11.512
We heard a commotion outside and locked the door.

45
08:12.513 --> 08:14.432
The culprit was hiding upstairs.

46
08:15.516 --> 08:17.476
How am I supposed to believe that?

47
08:21.272 --> 08:23.024
Here's my card.

48
08:24.400 --> 08:25.818
JOIL

49
08:27.361 --> 08:30.990
The president will be having dinner with the governor-general next week.

50
08:31.991 --> 08:32.992
That said,

51
08:33.075 --> 08:36.287
if he hears that the police pulled open the changing room curtain

52
08:37.288 --> 08:39.832
on his precious only daughter,

53
08:40.666 --> 08:43.794
I don't think he would be too happy.

54
08:57.224 --> 08:58.267
Sorry about that.

55
09:13.157 --> 09:14.367
Young-bok!

56
09:15.493 --> 09:16.327
Young-bok.

57
09:18.120 --> 09:20.122
Young-bok, stay with me.

58
09:21.916 --> 09:23.000
Young-bok.

59
09:30.966 --> 09:31.967
Miss.

60
09:32.677 --> 09:34.178
Are you all right?

61
09:37.223 --> 09:38.933
Oh no, Young-bok.

62
09:40.810 --> 09:41.686
Young-bok.

63
09:43.187 --> 09:45.106
Oh no, Young-bok!

64
09:55.032 --> 10:01.497
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

65
10:06.627 --> 10:09.714
I'm getting you in focus, so try not to move.

66
10:14.093 --> 10:16.345
This should work.

67
10:18.431 --> 10:19.890
Okay, here we go.

68
10:21.142 --> 10:22.560
Give me a smile.

69
10:24.186 --> 10:25.104
Good.

70
10:25.187 --> 10:27.523
One, two, three.

71
10:38.200 --> 10:39.118
What's the matter?

72
10:41.412 --> 10:42.788
No, it's nothing.

73
10:44.290 --> 10:46.709
I'm not sure I got the focus right.

74
10:48.085 --> 10:48.961
Excuse me.

75
10:49.670 --> 10:51.005
Would you mind helping me?

76
10:51.088 --> 10:52.089
Sorry?

77
10:52.173 --> 10:57.303
I forgot my glasses today, so I can't tell if the picture is blurry.

78
10:57.386 --> 10:58.721
I need your help.

79
10:59.680 --> 11:02.266
I'll adjust the distance.

80
11:02.349 --> 11:03.684
Just tell me when it looks clear.

81
11:04.769 --> 11:05.895
Sure, I can do that.

82
11:06.687 --> 11:08.481
Thank you. Here you go.

83
11:10.316 --> 11:13.444
Let's make this quick. I'm starving.

84
11:14.403 --> 11:17.531
I'll adjust it, so tell me when it looks clear to you.

85
11:19.450 --> 11:21.535
Give me a big smile.

86
11:29.585 --> 11:30.419
Okay.

87
11:32.630 --> 11:33.464
Is it clear?

88
11:36.008 --> 11:36.926
I'm not sure.

89
11:37.009 --> 11:38.135
Let's try again.

90
11:39.053 --> 11:40.554
Give me a smile.

91
11:46.852 --> 11:48.437
Are you still not sure?

92
11:52.691 --> 11:53.901
Seolleongtang delivery!

93
11:54.652 --> 11:55.778
Hold on a second.

94
11:58.447 --> 11:59.865
What took you so long?

95
12:00.366 --> 12:02.701
I've been having tons of delivery orders today.

96
12:02.785 --> 12:04.203
Ma'am, can I get some water?

97
12:04.286 --> 12:06.497
Sure, water's in the room back there.

98
12:06.580 --> 12:08.165
-Can I get two glasses? -Sure.

99
12:09.083 --> 12:10.626
-What are you-- -One moment.

100
12:18.175 --> 12:19.468
Must be crazy about each other.

101
12:25.558 --> 12:26.767
What are you doing?

102
12:28.018 --> 12:29.520
Just a moment.

103
12:38.946 --> 12:40.990
Come on, let's go.

104
12:43.284 --> 12:44.493
Okay, I'm coming!

105
12:47.913 --> 12:48.789
Still at it?

106
12:49.707 --> 12:51.166
-Thanks for the water, ma'am. -Sure.

107
12:51.250 --> 12:52.793
I'll come back for the bowls tomorrow.

108
12:53.377 --> 12:55.588
Thank you. See you.

109
12:55.671 --> 12:56.714
Bye.

110
12:57.590 --> 12:59.258
What took you so long?

111
12:59.925 --> 13:02.177
Sorry, I had to grab some water.

112
13:02.261 --> 13:03.304
Let's go home.

113
13:04.179 --> 13:05.890
No-ma, I want candy.

114
13:09.184 --> 13:10.519
Candy.

115
13:12.688 --> 13:14.064
Candy!

116
13:14.148 --> 13:15.024
All right.

117
13:20.779 --> 13:22.156
What was that all about?

118
13:25.743 --> 13:26.869
Did you cry?

119
13:30.247 --> 13:31.332
No, I just…

120
13:31.999 --> 13:33.959
got something in my eye.

121
13:46.513 --> 13:48.265
Who was that just now?

122
13:49.058 --> 13:49.934
A debt collector?

123
13:50.559 --> 13:51.393
Or…

124
13:52.645 --> 13:53.562
your former lover?

125
13:54.605 --> 13:55.731
What?

126
13:56.982 --> 13:58.275
A former lover?

127
13:58.359 --> 14:00.486
If not, why would you hide?

128
14:01.779 --> 14:03.197
What, were you afraid

129
14:04.114 --> 14:07.284
of running into him after cheating on him?

130
14:08.661 --> 14:09.870
Cheating?

131
14:13.457 --> 14:14.708
What do you take me for?

132
14:19.797 --> 14:20.756
Excuse me.

133
14:24.093 --> 14:25.177
Oh boy.

134
14:28.555 --> 14:29.473
I'm sorry.

135
14:32.476 --> 14:33.394
Ms. Keum.

136
14:36.480 --> 14:37.523
Ms. Keum!

137
14:48.492 --> 14:50.536
-How much is the candy? -One jeon.

138
14:57.918 --> 14:59.211
I'll take this one.

139
14:59.294 --> 15:00.838
Thank you.

140
15:03.173 --> 15:05.509
-Sir, please buy some candy. -Here.

141
15:08.721 --> 15:09.847
What's wrong?

142
15:10.806 --> 15:13.517
I just saw someone who looked like Ga-kyung.

143
15:16.520 --> 15:17.855
I told you, Kkot-nim.

144
15:17.938 --> 15:19.940
She's gone to America. Forget about her.

145
15:20.024 --> 15:21.025
You won't see her again.

146
15:21.108 --> 15:24.445
But I still miss her.

147
15:27.531 --> 15:28.490
Won't you eat your candy?

148
15:29.366 --> 15:30.993
I will.

149
15:31.076 --> 15:31.994
Go on then.

150
16:05.903 --> 16:06.904
Back off.

151
16:16.455 --> 16:17.331
Okay.

152
16:28.467 --> 16:29.384
Hold on.

153
16:47.444 --> 16:48.403
Move it over there.

154
17:13.095 --> 17:15.055
SUSPECT'S DESCRIPTION NAME: HAN CHEOL-YONG

155
17:17.432 --> 17:18.475
Look over here.

156
17:19.434 --> 17:20.269
Not him.

157
17:23.480 --> 17:24.314
Over that way!

158
17:25.274 --> 17:26.483
Spread out and search!

159
17:42.040 --> 17:44.293
Please let me go. My sister is waiting for me.

160
17:44.376 --> 17:45.544
Will you shut up?

161
17:50.966 --> 17:53.385
He's much older than me.

162
17:53.468 --> 17:54.636
Shut up.

163
17:57.973 --> 17:59.474
Kkot-nim is waiting for me.

164
18:07.941 --> 18:08.942
FOR KIDS' CONSTIPATION

165
18:10.694 --> 18:12.821
Sorry. I'm so sorry.

166
18:26.001 --> 18:27.085
Were you trying to pick this up?

167
18:30.672 --> 18:31.882
Is this yours?

168
18:31.965 --> 18:32.925
Here.

169
18:33.008 --> 18:34.509
Why are you here alone?

170
18:35.928 --> 18:37.054
Don't you have any family?

171
18:37.137 --> 18:39.890
I do have a family.

172
18:41.725 --> 18:43.393
I have an older sister

173
18:44.186 --> 18:46.230
and an older brother.

174
18:46.772 --> 18:51.235
My brother went to deliver seolleongtang, so I'm waiting for him.

175
18:52.611 --> 18:55.530
He said he'd be late if he took me along.

176
18:55.614 --> 18:57.991
So he promised he'd be quick.

177
19:00.577 --> 19:03.247
I've waited and waited,

178
19:04.164 --> 19:06.083
but he hasn't come back.

179
19:16.969 --> 19:18.470
I'm sorry I took so long.

180
19:19.513 --> 19:22.266
There are still police all over Jongno.

181
19:24.685 --> 19:26.186
What about Sato?

182
19:26.895 --> 19:28.105
Listen, Seok-jung.

183
19:28.897 --> 19:31.608
Forget about Sato for now. Take care of yourself first.

184
19:31.692 --> 19:34.653
You almost ended up six feet under before he did.

185
19:36.321 --> 19:38.573
In any case, we need to get you to a hospital.

186
19:40.993 --> 19:43.245
The trouble is, there are wanted posters at the hospital.

187
19:44.121 --> 19:46.498
Apparently, the Gugukdan targeted Sato

188
19:46.581 --> 19:48.500
in Dongsung-dong tonight but failed.

189
19:50.544 --> 19:52.713
Still, word is the Japanese police took heavy losses.

190
19:54.172 --> 19:56.091
The Gugukdan lost several members as well.

191
20:06.143 --> 20:07.102
Over there!

192
20:16.653 --> 20:20.157
My brother can run super fast.

193
20:21.450 --> 20:23.618
He used to pull a rickshaw.

194
20:23.702 --> 20:26.204
But these days, he delivers seolleongtang

195
20:26.997 --> 20:28.665
because he has a bicycle now.

196
20:29.374 --> 20:32.711
He couldn't ride a bike before,

197
20:33.920 --> 20:35.255
but now he rides well.

198
20:36.214 --> 20:40.302
He says he can deliver four bowls of seolleongtang at once.

199
20:40.385 --> 20:41.887
Wow, that's amazing.

200
20:42.471 --> 20:44.806
-Right? Isn't he cool? -He sure is.

201
20:44.890 --> 20:46.433
Mak-dung.

202
20:46.516 --> 20:48.185
-Mak-dung. Hurry, come eat. -Okay.

203
20:48.268 --> 20:51.980
My brother brought me seolleongtang the other day.

204
20:52.064 --> 20:53.607
It was really good.

205
20:53.690 --> 20:55.484
-Dad! -Dad!

206
20:57.444 --> 21:01.448
He says I'll get a stomachache if I eat too much seolleongtang,

207
21:01.531 --> 21:03.658
so I can only have it once a month.

208
21:04.159 --> 21:05.494
That's a lie.

209
21:06.078 --> 21:08.413
He's a terrible liar.

210
21:08.914 --> 21:11.792
My sister says it's because he has a good heart.

211
21:13.835 --> 21:15.295
We're here. That's our house.

212
21:42.656 --> 21:43.615
Aren't you hungry?

213
21:55.919 --> 21:57.587
Wow, that looks yummy!

214
22:00.632 --> 22:01.800
Careful, it's hot.

215
22:01.883 --> 22:02.968
I'll cool it down for you.

216
22:12.269 --> 22:14.896
Once you finish the porridge, take your cold medicine.

217
22:14.980 --> 22:17.107
Kkot-nim! Bang Kkot-nim!

218
22:18.150 --> 22:19.276
Bang Kkot-nim! Bang Kkot…

219
22:19.359 --> 22:20.402
Kkot-nim!

220
22:21.278 --> 22:22.654
-Where were you? -No-ma!

221
22:23.321 --> 22:24.406
Kkot-nim.

222
22:26.908 --> 22:29.327
How did you get home? And what are you eating?

223
22:29.411 --> 22:30.954
And who are you?

224
22:37.669 --> 22:39.546
I'm home.

225
22:48.513 --> 22:49.514
Is no one home?

226
23:02.986 --> 23:04.070
What?

227
23:04.154 --> 23:05.447
A former lover?

228
23:07.115 --> 23:08.074
Cheating?

229
23:09.493 --> 23:10.327
Unbelievable.

230
23:10.410 --> 23:13.997
A rich kid's mind really is a world of luxury.

231
23:14.080 --> 23:18.168
I couldn't even afford to beat the cold, let alone cheat on anybody.

232
23:23.798 --> 23:25.050
Oh dear.

233
23:26.218 --> 23:27.511
Kkot-nim.

234
23:29.513 --> 23:32.724
Why are you coughing? It breaks my heart.

235
23:48.990 --> 23:49.950
I suppose

236
23:50.867 --> 23:52.744
this is where it ends.

237
23:54.746 --> 23:56.289
-Take him away. -Yes, sir!

238
24:05.757 --> 24:08.134
Your plan worked brilliantly, sir.

239
24:09.469 --> 24:11.680
The Gugukdan really did turn up.

240
24:11.763 --> 24:14.266
The one behind the attack at Yoo Philip's house

241
24:14.349 --> 24:15.850
must be a member of the Gugukdan.

242
24:17.435 --> 24:20.772
Do you realize how many officers we lost just to kill one guy?

243
24:22.232 --> 24:23.775
Did you even count them?

244
24:26.778 --> 24:27.612
I'm sorry, sir.

245
24:27.696 --> 24:29.447
Hunt down every last one of them.

246
24:30.031 --> 24:31.700
Wipe out the Gugukdan for good.

247
24:33.535 --> 24:35.870
Get that guy first and round them all up.

248
24:39.499 --> 24:41.001
On it, sir!

249
24:43.920 --> 24:45.213
Inspector General!

250
24:45.839 --> 24:46.840
Chief!

251
24:47.924 --> 24:49.175
We caught him.

252
25:19.664 --> 25:20.582
Hands in the air.

253
25:23.460 --> 25:24.419
It's me.

254
25:41.519 --> 25:42.354
Are you hurt?

255
25:43.521 --> 25:44.898
Han Cheol-yong…

256
25:46.608 --> 25:47.484
is dead.

257
25:49.235 --> 25:51.363
The police have his body, so…

258
25:52.781 --> 25:54.908
in case the police come searching,

259
25:55.575 --> 25:58.244
I came to clear out his room.

260
26:03.500 --> 26:04.542
Is this everything?

261
26:05.251 --> 26:06.294
Yes.

262
26:06.378 --> 26:08.421
I think he cleaned it out beforehand.

263
26:09.172 --> 26:10.548
Let's get out of here then.

264
26:28.233 --> 26:30.110
No nation in the world

265
26:31.069 --> 26:34.322
has the right to occupy another country by force

266
26:34.989 --> 26:38.618
and oppress its people.

267
26:41.413 --> 26:45.375
The independence of our country is only right,

268
26:46.084 --> 26:47.669
and it will inevitably come to pass.

269
26:55.093 --> 26:57.011
Oh no, Jeong-yeop.

270
26:59.347 --> 27:00.849
Jeong-yeop.

271
27:04.853 --> 27:06.855
What in the world happened?

272
27:09.899 --> 27:11.443
Jeong-yeop!

273
27:11.526 --> 27:13.403
If my death could bring about

274
27:13.987 --> 27:17.449
the independence of my nation even a single second sooner,

275
27:20.368 --> 27:24.122
I hold no regrets at all.

276
27:25.832 --> 27:26.916
A man of Joseon.

277
27:28.042 --> 27:30.754
Han Cheol-yong.

278
28:06.372 --> 28:07.332
Madam.

279
28:18.718 --> 28:19.761
Madam.

280
28:29.062 --> 28:30.355
I'm coming in.

281
28:40.114 --> 28:41.825
Didn't she come home last night?

282
28:58.049 --> 28:59.384
Present arms!

283
29:07.809 --> 29:08.977
Welcome, sir.

284
29:10.144 --> 29:13.481
We didn't know you were returning to Keijo today, Your Excellency.

285
29:13.565 --> 29:15.149
How was your journey?

286
29:15.692 --> 29:18.236
About as peaceful as Keijo.

287
29:18.987 --> 29:22.448
With scoundrels like Lee Bong-chang and Lee Deok-ju around,

288
29:22.532 --> 29:25.743
I have to hide my itinerary and move around under the radar.

289
29:26.828 --> 29:29.038
You'd think I were some kind of criminal.

290
29:30.790 --> 29:34.419
So I hear there was a shootout near Keijo Imperial University yesterday.

291
29:34.502 --> 29:35.545
Did you catch the culprit?

292
29:36.880 --> 29:38.214
We shot one dead at the scene--

293
29:38.298 --> 29:39.465
Ever since you took office,

294
29:39.549 --> 29:41.467
it seems those subversives

295
29:41.551 --> 29:44.929
have been running rampant, don't you think?

296
30:12.540 --> 30:14.250
You can't die, Young-bok.

297
30:16.336 --> 30:18.421
You'd better not die, or you're fired.

298
30:24.302 --> 30:25.386
Who's there?

299
30:25.470 --> 30:27.805
Didn't I tell you to stay away from my room?

300
30:27.889 --> 30:29.098
Miss.

301
30:29.182 --> 30:30.892
Your father is leaving now.

302
30:54.707 --> 30:55.667
Father.

303
30:56.250 --> 30:57.710
Have a good day.

304
30:57.794 --> 30:59.253
All right.

305
31:02.882 --> 31:04.801
Young-bok, that ungrateful brat.

306
31:05.468 --> 31:06.678
I thought he was bright,

307
31:06.761 --> 31:08.763
so I sent him to school and made him my butler.

308
31:08.846 --> 31:10.098
Yet over a little stomach bug,

309
31:10.181 --> 31:12.558
he wouldn't bother to show up when I go to work?

310
31:14.102 --> 31:16.771
That's the problem with these lowborn sorts.

311
31:16.854 --> 31:18.064
I can't educate them.

312
31:18.147 --> 31:20.525
The king may say the classes are all equal now.

313
31:20.608 --> 31:22.652
But generations of slave blood run in his veins.

314
31:25.029 --> 31:28.157
Just because he piggybacked you as a kid and grew up beside you,

315
31:28.241 --> 31:29.867
he forgot he's some lowborn nobody.

316
31:30.535 --> 31:31.536
For crying out loud.

317
31:33.746 --> 31:36.708
You hang around the Japanese and think you're one of them now.

318
31:38.876 --> 31:39.877
What?

319
31:39.961 --> 31:41.379
What was that, Myung-nam?

320
31:43.256 --> 31:44.090
It's nothing.

321
31:44.173 --> 31:47.719
I'll give Young-bok a proper earful, so don't worry about it.

322
31:48.469 --> 31:50.847
Still, he's quite sick. I'll let him take three days off.

323
31:50.930 --> 31:52.181
Fine.

324
31:52.265 --> 31:55.101
But make sure those three days are unpaid.

325
31:55.727 --> 31:57.228
Sure, I'll handle it.

326
31:57.812 --> 31:59.230
Have a good day, Dad.

327
31:59.313 --> 32:00.273
You too.

328
32:13.494 --> 32:14.954
There you go.

329
32:15.621 --> 32:17.248
Let's get this medicine down.

330
32:20.543 --> 32:21.794
Down it goes.

331
32:22.879 --> 32:24.005
All gone.

332
32:24.088 --> 32:25.173
Good job.

333
32:27.592 --> 32:29.677
So this was medicine for constipation?

334
32:29.761 --> 32:31.179
That's right.

335
32:31.679 --> 32:34.932
We don't know how to read, so we had no idea what this was.

336
32:35.016 --> 32:35.850
Right?

337
32:39.353 --> 32:43.024
That's why Ga-kyung drew this for us before she left.

338
32:43.941 --> 32:45.777
I miss her.

339
32:49.572 --> 32:50.531
Tell me about it.

340
32:53.409 --> 32:56.162
Ga-kyung, seriously…

341
32:56.245 --> 32:58.081
-You know what? -Yeah?

342
32:58.164 --> 33:03.878
I think the teacher is the most handsome man I've ever seen.

343
33:03.961 --> 33:06.130
What? Who? That guy from yesterday?

344
33:06.214 --> 33:07.423
Yeah.

345
33:07.507 --> 33:11.302
Hey, he's pale as a ghost, like a walking tofu block.

346
33:11.385 --> 33:12.762
You call that handsome?

347
33:13.429 --> 33:15.014
And why are you calling him "teacher"?

348
33:15.098 --> 33:19.393
I asked him to teach me how to read, so he's my teacher.

349
33:19.477 --> 33:20.436
What?

350
33:21.813 --> 33:22.897
How to read?

351
33:22.980 --> 33:26.776
Yeah, he's going to come over to teach me how to read.

352
33:26.859 --> 33:28.111
He promised me.

353
33:28.194 --> 33:30.905
Kkot-nim, you should've asked me first!

354
33:31.697 --> 33:34.367
I can't wait for him to come.

355
33:34.992 --> 33:38.079
Now I get to learn how to read like Ga-kyung.

356
33:38.162 --> 33:39.372
I'm going to read!

357
33:39.455 --> 33:41.207
Hey, Bang Kkot-nim!

358
33:44.919 --> 33:47.088
I just hope the boss doesn't catch us.

359
34:10.153 --> 34:12.405
What? Did you have something to say?

360
34:13.072 --> 34:15.199
Things are tense at the Government-General today.

361
34:15.283 --> 34:16.993
So don't wander around if you can.

362
34:17.743 --> 34:19.871
You always tell me not to wander around.

363
34:21.289 --> 34:22.707
Can I not even go to the bathroom?

364
34:23.833 --> 34:26.127
I'm saying, don't wander around for no reason.

365
34:26.210 --> 34:28.212
I've never wandered around for no reason.

366
34:28.296 --> 34:30.590
The only ladies' room is in the corner on the first floor.

367
34:30.673 --> 34:32.049
So it just takes long.

368
34:32.133 --> 34:34.010
It's not like I'm slacking off.

369
34:34.719 --> 34:36.262
Very well, then.

370
34:36.929 --> 34:38.598
Speaking of which, I need to use the restroom.

371
34:39.182 --> 34:41.434
You don't need to report that.

372
34:46.939 --> 34:47.815
By the way…

373
34:50.651 --> 34:53.696
why are things tense around here?

374
34:59.285 --> 35:01.412
Last night…

375
35:06.626 --> 35:07.835
Yes, Sato speaking.

376
35:10.338 --> 35:12.215
Yes, it's almost done.

377
35:21.557 --> 35:22.725
You complete idiot!

378
35:23.601 --> 35:25.728
What the hell were you thinking, dropping this pipe?

379
35:27.438 --> 35:32.485
Even if you Josenjings work your whole lives, you can't afford this!

380
35:32.568 --> 35:34.904
-Sorry, sir! -I'm sorry!

381
35:34.987 --> 35:37.073
You'd better not put a scratch on it,

382
35:37.156 --> 35:39.951
or you'll pay with your lives!

383
35:41.452 --> 35:42.662
Do it properly!

384
35:42.745 --> 35:44.121
I'm going to the bathroom.

385
35:46.707 --> 35:48.751
NO ENTRY

386
35:58.469 --> 36:00.680
I hope that damn murderer drops dead in the street.

387
36:00.763 --> 36:02.890
All he ever says is "Josenjing."

388
36:03.474 --> 36:04.642
That wretched Japanese jerk.

389
36:04.725 --> 36:06.560
Hey, you okay after that beating?

390
36:06.644 --> 36:08.062
The same spot again, damn it.

391
36:14.819 --> 36:17.238
-Watch where you're going! -I'm sorry.

392
36:34.088 --> 36:37.008
Well, well, look who it is.

393
36:38.426 --> 36:39.760
Your name was…

394
36:41.470 --> 36:42.888
Yes, I'm Keum Seo-hee.

395
36:43.472 --> 36:46.017
It's an honor that you recall me.

396
36:47.643 --> 36:48.769
Keum Seo-hee.

397
36:48.853 --> 36:50.354
Right.

398
36:50.438 --> 36:53.149
I did hear you joined us as an interpreter trainee.

399
36:53.691 --> 36:57.111
I've been swamped and couldn't make time to come say hi.

400
36:57.194 --> 36:58.904
Don't worry about it, sir.

401
36:58.988 --> 37:01.073
I should have been the one to introduce myself.

402
37:02.366 --> 37:04.035
Is Mr. Yoo doing well?

403
37:04.702 --> 37:05.536
Yes, sir.

404
37:05.619 --> 37:09.165
If you have any trouble or need anything, feel free to come see me.

405
37:10.041 --> 37:11.459
Thank you very much.

406
37:13.210 --> 37:15.421
Joseon women are rather so boring.

407
37:17.089 --> 37:20.009
I suppose a woman educated by an American

408
37:21.510 --> 37:23.304
should be a bit different.

409
37:28.476 --> 37:29.685
Chief.

410
37:31.228 --> 37:32.438
Oh, Hideo.

411
37:33.856 --> 37:35.066
How have you been?

412
37:36.484 --> 37:37.651
Fine.

413
37:37.735 --> 37:38.903
It's been a while.

414
37:40.863 --> 37:43.699
This is Keum Seo-hee, an interpreter trainee.

415
37:43.783 --> 37:45.159
You've met her before, right?

416
37:47.161 --> 37:49.830
I'm sorry to interrupt your conversation,

417
37:49.914 --> 37:52.416
but I was looking for Ms. Keum. It's rather urgent.

418
37:54.543 --> 37:57.338
Please take this up to the Publications Division.

419
37:57.421 --> 37:58.422
It's on the fourth floor.

420
38:00.591 --> 38:01.801
Yes, sir.

421
38:10.101 --> 38:12.645
My apologies, Chief.

422
38:13.312 --> 38:15.064
It was an urgent matter.

423
38:17.149 --> 38:18.943
By the way, I heard there was a shootout

424
38:19.026 --> 38:21.278
with the Gugukdan in Dongsung-dong last night.

425
38:22.571 --> 38:25.991
I'm glad you weren't badly hurt.

426
38:28.702 --> 38:32.373
They came at us ready to die, yet all they managed was this tiny scratch.

427
38:34.583 --> 38:37.044
How is it working with Ms. Keum?

428
38:37.128 --> 38:42.133
As you know, I was ordered to make sure she was well taken care of.

429
38:43.551 --> 38:45.970
"Well taken care of," was it…

430
38:47.346 --> 38:49.890
Well, excuse me then.

431
38:56.397 --> 38:58.023
Two Josenjings…

432
38:59.400 --> 39:01.193
Well, isn't this interesting?

433
39:07.199 --> 39:08.200
Hideo.

434
39:10.619 --> 39:11.454
Yes?

435
39:17.751 --> 39:18.919
I'm back.

436
39:20.296 --> 39:22.923
I warned you not to wander around for no reason.

437
39:25.050 --> 39:28.429
I wasn't. I was just coming back from the bathroom.

438
39:30.055 --> 39:31.098
Last night…

439
39:33.726 --> 39:35.728
the Gugukdan tried to kill the inspector general

440
39:35.811 --> 39:37.021
near Keijo Imperial University.

441
39:38.397 --> 39:41.317
After the shootout, there were heavy casualties on both sides.

442
39:41.400 --> 39:43.611
We're hunting down the remaining fugitives.

443
39:52.536 --> 39:55.122
That's why things are tense around the office today.

444
39:59.543 --> 40:00.836
I see.

445
40:03.422 --> 40:04.256
Ms. Keum.

446
40:05.466 --> 40:06.300
Yes?

447
40:06.383 --> 40:08.552
You'll be working out of the office today.

448
40:09.637 --> 40:10.638
It's an order from above.

449
40:12.014 --> 40:13.140
Out of the office?

450
40:55.933 --> 41:00.437
JONGNO POLICE STATION

451
41:25.170 --> 41:26.255
-Sir! -Sir!

452
41:30.301 --> 41:32.678
Maybe this fool inside doesn't know Japanese.

453
41:32.761 --> 41:33.887
He hasn't said a word.

454
41:36.765 --> 41:40.311
I was going to call for a Joseon language interpreter.

455
41:41.854 --> 41:43.105
I'd appreciate your help.

456
41:43.939 --> 41:44.773
Sure.

457
41:45.691 --> 41:48.027
By the way…

458
41:49.403 --> 41:52.990
have you identified the fugitives who got away yesterday?

459
41:54.992 --> 41:56.368
Why do you want to know?

460
41:57.453 --> 42:01.707
I thought it might be useful while interpreting the interrogation.

461
42:01.790 --> 42:03.375
You don't need to know.

462
42:04.627 --> 42:05.461
Understood.

463
42:06.795 --> 42:09.089
Those bastards who ran took bullets.

464
42:10.007 --> 42:13.218
We're sweeping every hospital, so they'll get caught soon enough.

465
42:14.595 --> 42:15.846
-Open the door. -Yes, sir!

466
42:23.479 --> 42:24.480
Welcome, sir!

467
42:29.902 --> 42:30.778
Welcome.

468
42:32.237 --> 42:33.072
Come on in.

469
43:16.448 --> 43:20.536
Right after yesterday's shootout, we spotted a suspicious guy in Jongno

470
43:20.619 --> 43:23.914
and combed the whole neighborhood. Then we found him hiding.

471
43:24.540 --> 43:26.166
Neither one has spoken yet,

472
43:26.250 --> 43:27.835
but he fits the description

473
43:27.918 --> 43:30.546
of the suspect who broke into the American reporter's house.

474
43:31.797 --> 43:34.007
His old gunshot wound

475
43:34.925 --> 43:36.385
is badly infected,

476
43:36.927 --> 43:38.971
so he's burning up with a fever.

477
43:52.735 --> 43:53.861
How are you?

478
43:54.820 --> 43:55.696
What's your name?

479
44:02.953 --> 44:03.787
Interpret that.

480
44:05.622 --> 44:06.582
Yes, sir.

481
44:08.292 --> 44:09.835
What is your name?

482
44:22.890 --> 44:24.975
If you won't talk on your own,

483
44:25.058 --> 44:26.935
I'll have no choice but to make you.

484
44:28.061 --> 44:28.896
Go ahead.

485
44:59.968 --> 45:01.220
Why are you out here?

486
45:01.303 --> 45:02.471
Jeez, you scared me.

487
45:02.554 --> 45:05.599
I thought you were a ghost from the crematorium.

488
45:05.682 --> 45:07.476
You almost gave me a heart attack.

489
45:08.560 --> 45:10.187
And stop talking nonsense.

490
45:10.813 --> 45:14.566
That's a crematorium for the Jap. Why would a Japanese ghost come here?

491
45:14.650 --> 45:17.444
It's all Gyodang-ri, either here or there.

492
45:17.528 --> 45:18.445
Yeah, right.

493
45:19.696 --> 45:20.906
Look at this.

494
45:20.989 --> 45:21.907
Right here.

495
45:22.574 --> 45:25.285
This is what the Japs did just because we cried for independence.

496
45:25.369 --> 45:28.163
But they're all from the same Gyodang-ri? Like hell.

497
45:30.916 --> 45:33.126
-What are you doing out here? -What?

498
45:34.044 --> 45:35.546
Did something happen to Kkot-nim?

499
45:35.629 --> 45:36.839
No, not at all.

500
45:37.756 --> 45:40.801
I was just out watching the stars.

501
45:42.135 --> 45:44.638
You'll just get hungry if you stay up. Go to sleep.

502
45:45.639 --> 45:47.349
Okay, good night.

503
45:49.184 --> 45:51.186
I thought the boss had caught us.

504
45:53.689 --> 45:57.025
You pale tofu. Don't you dare try something funny.

505
45:57.109 --> 45:58.151
Giyeok.

506
45:58.652 --> 45:59.486
Giyeok.

507
46:01.071 --> 46:02.197
Giyeok.

508
46:15.210 --> 46:17.754
Teacher, is something wrong?

509
46:17.838 --> 46:18.714
What?

510
46:19.298 --> 46:21.174
No, nothing's wrong.

511
46:21.258 --> 46:24.344
I don't believe you. You look so worried.

512
46:25.971 --> 46:26.889
Not at all.

513
46:27.931 --> 46:29.016
Are you done writing?

514
46:29.099 --> 46:30.726
-Let's see. -Teacher.

515
46:30.809 --> 46:34.187
You should go. I can see it all over your face.

516
46:34.938 --> 46:35.772
Go where?

517
46:40.360 --> 46:44.698
You've been wanting to go to the bathroom. Am I right?

518
46:50.037 --> 46:53.999
The League of Nations Commission will soon arrive in Keijo.

519
46:54.082 --> 46:57.836
To have the League of Nations recognize Manchukuo's legitimacy,

520
46:58.337 --> 47:02.090
it is crucial that we show the Commission

521
47:02.174 --> 47:06.053
that Manchuria and Joseon are thriving in peace and prosperity.

522
47:06.887 --> 47:07.721
-Yes, sir. -Yes, sir.

523
47:08.889 --> 47:11.516
But in Manchuria,

524
47:12.059 --> 47:14.937
the Japanese army is being pushed around

525
47:15.020 --> 47:18.941
by rebels like Ji Cheong-cheon and Yang Se-bong.

526
47:19.024 --> 47:21.777
And Kim Gu's stooges

527
47:21.860 --> 47:26.490
are sneaking into Joseon to kill me.

528
47:27.532 --> 47:29.201
Until the Commission arrives,

529
47:29.284 --> 47:32.829
the Government-General's top priority

530
47:32.913 --> 47:35.123
is to maintain public order in Keijo.

531
47:35.207 --> 47:36.083
Is that clear?

532
47:36.166 --> 47:37.542
-Yes, sir! -Yes, sir!

533
47:37.626 --> 47:38.752
Inspector General.

534
47:40.337 --> 47:41.505
You should see to it

535
47:41.588 --> 47:46.510
that the foreign press in Keijo is handled with extreme care.

536
47:47.094 --> 47:51.014
Japan's deployment of the Kwantung Army to Manchuria

537
47:51.515 --> 47:55.435
was a legitimate act of retaliation

538
47:55.519 --> 47:59.189
against China's interference with Japanese economic activity.

539
47:59.272 --> 48:00.649
Make that clear to the press.

540
48:01.608 --> 48:02.442
Understood.

541
48:03.819 --> 48:04.778
You may go.

542
48:09.700 --> 48:10.534
Yes, sir.

543
48:23.588 --> 48:24.464
Commander.

544
48:24.548 --> 48:25.424
Yes, sir.

545
48:26.091 --> 48:30.512
Do you think he fully understood what I just said?

546
48:30.595 --> 48:31.638
Your Excellency.

547
48:32.222 --> 48:35.183
The Japanese in Joseon are colonial residents.

548
48:35.267 --> 48:36.893
They aren't mainlanders like us.

549
48:37.477 --> 48:40.731
Colonial residents are an inferior, lowborn lot.

550
48:41.231 --> 48:44.192
Men like him can scrub all they want,

551
48:44.276 --> 48:47.446
but they can't get the filth out from under their nails.

552
48:47.529 --> 48:50.574
You should be especially wary of them.

553
48:51.700 --> 48:52.659
Very well.

554
48:53.160 --> 48:54.327
That's right.

555
49:01.543 --> 49:04.379
These Josenjings are like cockroaches.

556
49:04.463 --> 49:06.757
No matter how many we crush, they keep crawling back.

557
49:07.340 --> 49:09.426
Is this your stubborn nature?

558
49:09.509 --> 49:12.971
Did you think we'd be impressed and hand you your independence?

559
49:18.351 --> 49:19.394
What are you doing?

560
49:19.936 --> 49:20.937
Interpret that.

561
49:21.021 --> 49:21.897
Yes.

562
49:24.107 --> 49:25.025
He says

563
49:25.984 --> 49:29.029
that people of Joseon continue to fight for independence.

564
49:31.281 --> 49:32.240
That's it?

565
49:32.324 --> 49:34.117
Why was that so short?

566
49:35.660 --> 49:36.870
I'm sorry.

567
49:37.412 --> 49:39.539
I was trying to find the right Joseon words

568
49:39.623 --> 49:40.707
to capture your meaning.

569
49:43.210 --> 49:46.838
He's asking if you think this will ever lead to independence.

570
49:48.632 --> 49:51.426
There's something I'm genuinely curious about.

571
49:51.510 --> 49:54.679
Do you, independence fighters, the Gugukdan or whatever,

572
49:54.763 --> 49:57.140
honestly believe you can save Joseon?

573
49:57.766 --> 49:59.059
He's asking if you think

574
49:59.142 --> 50:01.812
the independence fighters can save Joseon.

575
50:03.772 --> 50:05.982
Don't you want to answer, or don't you know?

576
50:07.317 --> 50:09.069
Then I'll tell you.

577
50:11.738 --> 50:12.906
You…

578
50:12.989 --> 50:15.867
Your so-called independence movement is ruining Joseon.

579
50:16.827 --> 50:19.621
You're holding on to a dead hope

580
50:19.704 --> 50:22.290
and instigating the barbaric Josenjings.

581
50:22.791 --> 50:26.545
You traitors are robbing them of the honor of being reborn

582
50:27.379 --> 50:29.714
as loyal subjects of the Great Empire of Japan.

583
50:31.049 --> 50:33.718
Do you realize how pathetic it is

584
50:34.427 --> 50:36.721
to cling to a hope that's already dead?

585
50:42.686 --> 50:43.979
The independence fighters

586
50:44.688 --> 50:46.690
are ruining Joseon.

587
50:47.607 --> 50:49.818
You're holding on to a long-dead hope,

588
50:50.652 --> 50:51.820
instigating barbaric--

589
50:51.903 --> 50:53.572
Why is it taking you so long?

590
50:55.282 --> 50:56.992
You're instigating the barbaric Josenj…

591
50:57.075 --> 50:58.702
people of Joseon.

592
50:58.785 --> 51:01.079
You're committing treason by robbing them of the chance

593
51:01.163 --> 51:03.623
of being reborn as subjects of the Great Empire of Japan.

594
51:15.427 --> 51:17.220
You pathetic Josenjing.

595
51:17.304 --> 51:21.308
I bet you felt like a hero while plotting your grand scheme.

596
51:23.185 --> 51:24.686
But look at you now.

597
51:24.769 --> 51:25.937
Look around this room.

598
51:26.730 --> 51:28.398
Who do you have around you?

599
51:29.941 --> 51:32.277
Did you promise to keep your mouth shut if you got caught?

600
51:35.906 --> 51:37.282
Did you take an oath or something?

601
51:38.408 --> 51:42.329
Now you're learning the hard way

602
51:43.121 --> 51:46.875
how pointless an oath made by lowborn scum like you actually is!

603
51:50.253 --> 51:51.504
Your grand scheme…

604
51:52.631 --> 51:53.715
Do you understand me?

605
51:55.383 --> 51:57.719
A miserable, meaningless death all alone.

606
51:58.595 --> 52:01.264
That's all the Josenjing independence movement will ever achieve.

607
52:03.391 --> 52:05.310
I said, do you understand?

608
52:05.393 --> 52:08.271
You filthy Josenjing roaches.

609
52:12.025 --> 52:13.944
Why isn't he saying anything?

610
52:15.278 --> 52:17.656
Are you interpreting my words properly?

611
52:17.739 --> 52:19.616
Interpreter trainee Keum Seo-hee.

612
52:23.119 --> 52:25.580
Interpreter trainee Keum Seo-hee!

613
52:35.340 --> 52:36.383
Who are you?

614
52:39.511 --> 52:40.762
You.

615
52:41.763 --> 52:43.265
You're that live-in maid, aren't you?

616
52:47.269 --> 52:49.396
Why are you using that name?

617
52:50.021 --> 52:50.855
Why?

618
52:54.192 --> 52:55.819
What is he talking about?

619
52:55.902 --> 52:57.153
What are you all doing?

620
52:57.237 --> 52:58.989
Is that your real name?

621
52:59.572 --> 53:01.199
Is that really your name?

622
53:01.866 --> 53:03.868
Who the hell are you?

623
53:07.539 --> 53:09.207
Answer me!

624
53:09.291 --> 53:11.918
Why are you using her name?

625
53:15.130 --> 53:16.965
What's this lunatic saying now?

626
53:17.048 --> 53:18.967
Who are you really?

627
53:19.551 --> 53:21.845
I said, who are you?

628
53:21.928 --> 53:23.888
Interpret that, Keum Seo-hee!

629
53:39.029 --> 53:40.947
Why, Interpreter Sato.

630
53:41.614 --> 53:43.616
What brings you all the way here?

631
53:48.621 --> 53:49.539
By any chance,

632
53:50.040 --> 53:52.417
did you come by to check on Ms. Keum?

633
53:54.169 --> 53:56.838
I'm here to see if the work is being handled properly.

634
53:59.299 --> 54:02.218
As you can see, she's--

635
54:02.302 --> 54:03.178
No.

636
54:04.804 --> 54:06.264
I'm talking about you, Chief.

637
54:07.766 --> 54:12.020
I'd like to hear what you've found out from him so far.

638
54:12.937 --> 54:15.565
You pulled an English interpreter trainee

639
54:15.648 --> 54:19.819
from the Foreign Affairs Division to interrogate in the Joseon language.

640
54:20.987 --> 54:24.449
I suppose you've found out quite a lot by now.

641
54:27.243 --> 54:28.203
Well, then,

642
54:28.286 --> 54:29.829
tell me what you've found out.

643
54:30.413 --> 54:33.416
What was his motive for targeting the inspector general?

644
54:33.500 --> 54:35.043
What is his name?

645
54:35.126 --> 54:37.212
What did you find out about the Gugukdan?

646
54:39.672 --> 54:41.424
You insolent Josenjing!

647
54:42.050 --> 54:45.804
How dare a mere interpreter speak to me like that!

648
54:47.806 --> 54:49.391
I've spoiled you like a young master,

649
54:49.474 --> 54:52.060
and now you seem to have forgotten your place.

650
54:52.143 --> 54:55.480
Do you really think you're the inspector general's son?

651
54:56.189 --> 54:58.316
You're nothing but a Josenj…

652
55:08.952 --> 55:10.495
Inspector General.

653
55:20.463 --> 55:22.507
-When did you get here-- -Finish what you were saying.

654
55:26.428 --> 55:27.679
I'm intrigued.

655
55:28.763 --> 55:30.598
If Hideo isn't my real son,

656
55:33.726 --> 55:34.561
then what is he?

657
55:43.903 --> 55:45.071
Please forgive me!

658
55:45.572 --> 55:47.449
Please forgive my outburst, sir!

659
55:55.874 --> 55:57.000
I apologize for the trouble.

660
55:59.586 --> 56:01.337
Make sure she gets home safely.

661
56:01.421 --> 56:02.380
Interpreter Sato.

662
56:38.833 --> 56:41.127
Sir, please allow me to explain--

663
56:46.591 --> 56:47.717
Forgive me, sir!

664
56:47.800 --> 56:51.054
Did you forget Keum Seo-hee is involved with that American reporter?

665
56:52.430 --> 56:53.765
Did you forget how critical

666
56:53.848 --> 56:57.352
foreign press coverage of Joseon is because of Manchukuo?

667
56:59.437 --> 57:03.358
You learned nothing from what happened in 1919.

668
57:06.861 --> 57:07.862
Did you forget

669
57:08.780 --> 57:11.032
how "that incident" blew up

670
57:11.115 --> 57:13.117
after the Americans reported it abroad?

671
57:14.160 --> 57:15.328
I am deeply sorry, sir.

672
57:19.123 --> 57:20.416
Utter idiot.

673
57:44.899 --> 57:45.817
Ms. Keum.

674
57:51.406 --> 57:52.323
My apologies.

675
57:54.325 --> 57:56.119
I assure you it won't happen again.

676
58:02.292 --> 58:03.209
That being said…

677
58:07.005 --> 58:08.131
I'd appreciate it…

678
58:11.050 --> 58:12.719
if today's incident didn't reach

679
58:14.637 --> 58:15.805
the foreign press.

680
58:20.059 --> 58:21.561
I mean, Mr. Yoo.

681
58:52.634 --> 58:54.218
Have you found out who he is?

682
58:54.302 --> 58:56.054
Not yet, sir. My apologies.

683
58:57.597 --> 58:58.723
But he keeps insisting

684
58:59.223 --> 59:02.852
that he and that man are not members of the Gugukdan.

685
59:04.354 --> 59:05.647
We'll find out soon.

686
59:05.730 --> 59:08.316
I'd prefer if they were the Gugukdan.

687
59:11.903 --> 59:14.656
Did you know your fellow members were killed in Dongsung-dong?

688
59:21.204 --> 59:22.830
We've identified him, sir.

689
59:22.914 --> 59:23.998
Is that so?

690
59:24.082 --> 59:26.125
Yes, we found him in the watchlist files.

691
59:26.209 --> 59:27.543
His name is Na Byeong-sun.

692
59:27.627 --> 59:29.671
He lives in Anseong-gun, Gyeonggi Province.

693
59:30.755 --> 59:31.589
See?

694
59:32.173 --> 59:33.800
You can hold your tongue all you want,

695
59:33.883 --> 59:35.760
but we find everything out eventually.

696
59:36.344 --> 59:38.596
What's the point of wasting time like this?

697
59:39.889 --> 59:41.849
Bring his wife and children here. Now.

698
59:41.933 --> 59:42.809
Yes, sir.

699
59:46.479 --> 59:49.065
Let's see if he'll stay quiet once we put his family

700
59:49.148 --> 59:50.525
hanging in front of him.

701
59:58.282 --> 01:00:00.368
You'd better start talking.

702
01:00:00.451 --> 01:00:01.869
Unless you want to watch

703
01:00:01.953 --> 01:00:04.455
your family die in front of you.

704
01:00:06.958 --> 01:00:08.376
My family?

705
01:00:29.522 --> 01:00:30.815
Shut up!

706
01:00:47.832 --> 01:00:50.168
So it won't leak to foreign outlets?

707
01:00:50.918 --> 01:00:51.961
Yes.

708
01:00:54.005 --> 01:00:55.173
If news of this

709
01:00:56.966 --> 01:00:58.593
gets out overseas,

710
01:00:59.927 --> 01:01:01.053
it could be a problem…

711
01:01:05.266 --> 01:01:07.393
Mr. Yoo is a journalist, after all.

712
01:01:10.396 --> 01:01:11.606
I'd appreciate your discretion.

713
01:01:19.322 --> 01:01:20.740
Understood.

714
01:01:22.992 --> 01:01:25.620
Thank you for kindly reminding me how I became

715
01:01:25.703 --> 01:01:28.331
an interpreter trainee at the Government-General.

716
01:01:32.502 --> 01:01:33.878
Thank you for everything.

717
01:01:35.254 --> 01:01:37.131
-Ms. Keum. -I'll go by myself.

718
01:02:43.614 --> 01:02:45.616
What, are you going somewhere?

719
01:02:45.700 --> 01:02:48.327
I'm done playing spy. Goodbye.

720
01:02:48.411 --> 01:02:49.871
You're quitting?

721
01:02:49.954 --> 01:02:50.955
Yes!

722
01:02:51.038 --> 01:02:52.540
I quit.

723
01:02:52.623 --> 01:02:55.501
I shouldn't have gotten involved in this mess in the first place.

724
01:02:56.002 --> 01:02:57.879
I don't want to die for nothing.

725
01:02:59.171 --> 01:03:00.131
"Die for nothing"?

726
01:03:00.214 --> 01:03:02.258
Right, for nothing.

727
01:03:02.967 --> 01:03:05.636
Look, you went to Dongsung-dong yesterday, didn't you?

728
01:03:06.512 --> 01:03:07.597
When I found out,

729
01:03:07.680 --> 01:03:10.391
I wondered if you'd been dead or arrested.

730
01:03:10.474 --> 01:03:13.477
I went to Jongno Police Station today worried sick about you.

731
01:03:13.561 --> 01:03:16.689
I could barely catch my breath until I realized it wasn't you.

732
01:03:17.648 --> 01:03:20.902
But do you know what I had to do there today?

733
01:03:22.737 --> 01:03:26.282
I interpreted the interrogation of a captured independence fighter.

734
01:03:29.243 --> 01:03:31.245
"You damn Josenjing."

735
01:03:31.787 --> 01:03:34.874
"I bet you felt like a hero while plotting your grand scheme."

736
01:03:34.957 --> 01:03:37.168
"But look at you now. Who do you have around you?"

737
01:03:37.251 --> 01:03:39.337
"You'll die for nothing all alone."

738
01:03:39.420 --> 01:03:42.256
"That's all the Josenjing independence movement will ever achieve."

739
01:03:42.340 --> 01:03:44.842
"You filthy Josenjing roaches!"

740
01:03:46.469 --> 01:03:48.012
I spent the whole day

741
01:03:49.013 --> 01:03:51.057
having to translate those insults.

742
01:03:51.724 --> 01:03:54.435
The man they'd arrested wouldn't say a single word.

743
01:03:54.518 --> 01:03:56.604
I was the only one talking back and forth

744
01:03:56.687 --> 01:03:58.773
between the chief of police and that man.

745
01:04:00.107 --> 01:04:01.984
I didn't know you'd be put in that position.

746
01:04:02.068 --> 01:04:03.027
But did you think

747
01:04:04.153 --> 01:04:06.155
being a spy was all fun and games?

748
01:04:09.492 --> 01:04:12.203
You said you didn't care about the independence movement.

749
01:04:12.286 --> 01:04:14.914
Then why take it so hard that you interpreted those words

750
01:04:14.997 --> 01:04:16.374
for an independence fighter?

751
01:04:18.000 --> 01:04:19.585
Who says I'm taking it hard?

752
01:04:19.669 --> 01:04:20.836
I'm not.

753
01:04:20.920 --> 01:04:23.631
It's just that once my cover gets blown,

754
01:04:23.714 --> 01:04:26.467
I'll end up arrested like him and killed for nothing.

755
01:04:26.550 --> 01:04:30.596
I refuse to die a meaningless death. So I'm out right here and now.

756
01:04:30.680 --> 01:04:31.931
Watch your mouth!

757
01:04:32.932 --> 01:04:34.183
"A meaningless death"?

758
01:04:36.018 --> 01:04:38.521
How can you say that about someone who was captured

759
01:04:38.604 --> 01:04:40.564
fighting for our nation's independence?

760
01:04:44.652 --> 01:04:47.697
No Joseon person would ever call that sacrifice meaningless.

761
01:04:47.780 --> 01:04:49.407
In fact, anywhere in the world,

762
01:04:49.490 --> 01:04:51.575
dying for your country's freedom

763
01:04:51.659 --> 01:04:53.577
is never considered a meaningless death.

764
01:04:54.161 --> 01:04:55.663
Don't kid yourself.

765
01:04:56.580 --> 01:04:58.624
I'm no independence fighter.

766
01:04:59.125 --> 01:05:00.126
You see,

767
01:05:00.209 --> 01:05:03.629
I took the job at the Government-General since you promised to send me to America.

768
01:05:03.713 --> 01:05:06.090
But if my cover gets blown,

769
01:05:06.173 --> 01:05:09.260
I'll look like an independence fighter in their eyes.

770
01:05:09.343 --> 01:05:12.096
How am I different from the man they interrogated today?

771
01:05:12.179 --> 01:05:15.766
I was posing as an interpreter trainee, and he was posing as a deliveryman.

772
01:05:15.850 --> 01:05:16.976
That's the only difference.

773
01:05:17.059 --> 01:05:18.310
It's the same thing!

774
01:05:19.854 --> 01:05:20.688
A deliveryman?

775
01:05:20.771 --> 01:05:21.647
Yes.

776
01:05:21.731 --> 01:05:22.857
It was him.

777
01:05:22.940 --> 01:05:25.401
The one who got into this house posing as a deliveryman.

778
01:05:27.069 --> 01:05:29.530
No matter how well you cover your tracks--

779
01:05:29.613 --> 01:05:30.573
You mean…

780
01:05:32.324 --> 01:05:34.452
he was the one who came here to kill Sato?

781
01:05:34.535 --> 01:05:35.703
Right.

782
01:05:36.245 --> 01:05:37.872
On the night of the dinner,

783
01:05:37.955 --> 01:05:39.582
he came into this house with a gun

784
01:05:39.665 --> 01:05:41.792
disguised as a deliveryman from Itsukoshi.

785
01:05:41.876 --> 01:05:43.669
He's not part of the Gugukdan, is he?

786
01:05:43.753 --> 01:05:44.628
Did he…

787
01:05:47.131 --> 01:05:48.841
say something?

788
01:05:50.968 --> 01:05:52.636
What did he say?

789
01:05:52.720 --> 01:05:53.804
Say?

790
01:05:54.346 --> 01:05:56.098
I wish he had said a single word.

791
01:05:56.182 --> 01:05:57.349
He wasn't cooperative at all.

792
01:05:57.433 --> 01:05:58.934
So the interrogation took all day.

793
01:05:59.810 --> 01:06:02.605
It was like he was set on keeping his mouth shut.

794
01:06:02.688 --> 01:06:04.231
That is, until he heard my name.

795
01:06:04.315 --> 01:06:07.276
All of a sudden, he started asking who I was.

796
01:06:07.359 --> 01:06:10.780
He went wild and yelled about why I was using that name.

797
01:06:14.158 --> 01:06:15.034
Your name?

798
01:06:17.161 --> 01:06:18.204
Lee Ga-kyung?

799
01:06:18.913 --> 01:06:19.747
What?

800
01:06:20.873 --> 01:06:21.749
No.

801
01:06:22.249 --> 01:06:23.667
Keum Seo-hee, obviously.

802
01:06:30.549 --> 01:06:32.510
The moment he heard that name, he started…

803
01:06:42.228 --> 01:06:43.062
What's going on?

804
01:06:54.907 --> 01:06:56.117
Seo-hee

805
01:06:56.826 --> 01:06:58.327
was my daughter's name.

806
01:07:00.871 --> 01:07:03.415
My daughter, the one killed by the inspector general.

807
01:07:08.629 --> 01:07:09.547
Don't tell me…

808
01:07:11.423 --> 01:07:12.299
Is he…

809
01:07:16.428 --> 01:07:18.681
your husband?

810
01:07:23.769 --> 01:07:26.063
Your daughter, Keum Seo-hee.

811
01:07:27.773 --> 01:07:30.109
Is he the father of your daughter?

812
01:07:31.777 --> 01:07:32.611
Is he?

813
01:07:35.865 --> 01:07:36.824
Is he really?

814
01:07:38.117 --> 01:07:39.952
Is that true? Really?

815
01:07:58.721 --> 01:08:00.806
You people are insane!

816
01:08:01.390 --> 01:08:03.475
Is independence really worth all this?

817
01:08:03.559 --> 01:08:06.020
You're here like this, and your husband…

818
01:08:06.103 --> 01:08:09.148
He's lying there covered in blood, beaten half to death.

819
01:08:12.776 --> 01:08:15.362
I'm not dying getting caught up in this madness.

820
01:08:16.030 --> 01:08:18.365
I'm out. I'm calling it quits.

821
01:08:18.449 --> 01:08:21.243
I told you. There's no mercy for traitors.

822
01:08:21.327 --> 01:08:22.786
Go right ahead.

823
01:08:23.621 --> 01:08:25.789
You made me a spy, but you never trusted me.

824
01:08:25.873 --> 01:08:28.167
What kind of spy is that? And what did I betray?

825
01:08:28.250 --> 01:08:30.127
-Lee Ga-kyung. -Get your hands off me!

826
01:08:38.385 --> 01:08:40.554
This is insane.

827
01:08:55.444 --> 01:08:56.278
Oh no.

828
01:08:58.364 --> 01:08:59.323
No.

829
01:09:25.516 --> 01:09:27.101
Why's everything such a mess?

830
01:09:55.504 --> 01:09:56.463
Keum Seo-hee.

831
01:10:13.355 --> 01:10:14.565
Who?

832
01:10:15.316 --> 01:10:17.151
I don't know anyone by that name.

833
01:11:12.039 --> 01:11:18.670
A MAN OF JOSEON HAN CHEOL-YONG

834
01:11:18.754 --> 01:11:22.674
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

835
01:11:22.758 --> 01:11:23.926
Keum Seo-hee.

836
01:11:24.885 --> 01:11:26.845
She's going to rely on you a lot.

837
01:11:28.222 --> 01:11:29.098
INTERPRETER SATO HIDEO

838
01:11:29.181 --> 01:11:30.099
Seo-hee's father.

839
01:11:30.182 --> 01:11:31.558
What are you planning to do?

840
01:11:31.642 --> 01:11:33.310
What Sato wants to hide the most…

841
01:11:34.103 --> 01:11:35.771
A mass murderer.

842
01:11:35.854 --> 01:11:38.649
If Sato realizes he was one of the victims from the Kyeam-ri massacre,

843
01:11:38.732 --> 01:11:41.443
there's a chance he'll find out who I am.

844
01:11:43.278 --> 01:11:44.446
Keum Seo-hee.

845
01:11:44.530 --> 01:11:46.532
Win Sato Hideo's heart.

846
01:11:46.615 --> 01:11:47.866
Get him on your side.

847
01:11:48.826 --> 01:11:51.620
Should I end things with Mr. Yoo?

848
01:11:51.703 --> 01:11:53.455
She needs to trust you, but…

849
01:11:53.539 --> 01:11:54.373
Ms. Keum!

850
01:11:54.456 --> 01:11:56.583
Never let yourself have personal feelings.

851
01:12:04.049 --> 01:12:06.051
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
